# Cloudflare Pages response headers.
#
# Vite copies public/ verbatim into dist/, so this file ships with every deploy.
# Pages parses it and never serves it as an asset.
#
# ── Why the rules look like this ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Matching rules MERGE, and a header set by two matching rules is joined with a
# comma — so a catch-all Cache-Control plus a specific one would produce
# something like "public, max-age=0, must-revalidate, public, max-age=31536000,
# immutable". That is why the asset rule detaches (leading "!") the catch-all
# value before setting its own, instead of merely layering underneath it.
#
# ── The policy ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Two kinds of thing are served and they want opposite treatment:
#
#   1. The app shell — /index.html, and /200.html which is the SPA fallback
#      reached at every extensionless route. It names the hashed bundles, so a
#      stale copy means running an older app, possibly against a newer API.
#      Pinned to revalidate: a browser may keep a copy but must check with the
#      server before using it, so a deploy can never be invisible to someone
#      who navigates during it.
#
#   2. Everything under /assets/. Vite puts a content hash in every filename, so
#      the bytes at a given name never change and a new build always produces a
#      new name. There is nothing to go stale, so these are cached for a year
#      and never revalidated — which also removes a round trip per asset on
#      every load.
#
# ── Robots ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Reading the archive is public, so the app is meant to be findable. This header
# used to be `noindex, nofollow`, from when the whole app belonged to the owner.
# The finer-grained policy lives in `robots.txt`, because every route serves
# this same shell and cannot be targeted here individually.
/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache, max-age=0, must-revalidate
  X-Robots-Tag: all
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin

/assets/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
